  "worked_solution": "The point $C$ is in the fourth quadrant, so statement I is false.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the point $C,$ we start at the origin, move $3$ units *right* and then $2$ units *down*. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14162111/assets/98c5cd8e245651f99a29c37b6d63122fa7766eed80c64ab6870e05192742dab1.png)\n\nThe coordinates of $C$ are $(3,-2).$ Hence, statements II and III are true.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
